Costco's membership fees were $5,323 in 2025, up from $4,828 in 2024 and $4,580 in 2023 [1] (in millions, per the filing's tables). Membership fee revenue increased 10% in 2025, driven by new member sign-ups and membership fee increases. [2]

On the fee increase specifically, Costco raised annual membership fees in the U.S. and Canada effective September 1, 2024, and the fee income increase accounted for approximately 40% of membership income growth during 2025. [2] Because membership fees are recognized ratably over the one-year membership period [2], the increase flows through gradually.

Member growth also contributed: total paid members rose to 81,000 thousand in 2025 from 76,200 thousand in 2024 [3]. Renewal rates were a partial offset: they stood at 92.3% in the U.S. and Canada and 89.8% worldwide, and were negatively affected by more memberships sold online, including through digital promotions, which renew at a slightly lower rate on average. [2]